> ought to be the same, yet they are not ...

If you do similar preprocessing and normalization steps, you may still
see small differences due to what model estimators/algorithms are
used.  There are several options ('flavor') in aroma.affymetrix that
allows you do produce results that are numerically very close to what
other produces (this hasn't been verified for RMAExpress though).  See
also the recent aroma.affymetrix thread "RMA of aroma.affymetrix,
affyPLM and affy" started Aug 4, 2009.

>
> I asked my mentor about this question of "inconsistency", and showed
