It looks like the *.Rcache file is corrupt.  I have never seen this,
but I can imagine several reasons causing it, e.g. the file is not
accessible, incomplete due to a full disk and so on.  This may be that
this is the cause of your problem of not obtaining regions for all
chromosomes.

I have updated the R.cache package so that it reports the pathname of
the broken cache file.  Update to R.cache v0.1.8 by:

source("http://www.braju.com/R/hbLite.R");
hbLite("R.cache");

and rerun your script.

If the problem persist, you should then get error messages such as:

[2009-08-11 16:37:23] Exception: Rcache file format error. Read empty
header identifier: '~/.Rcache/e6ddd8a99035bdcfd337437a930ba19b.Rcache'
[description of the opened connection]

Then cut'n'paste the pathname displayed and see what:

print(file.info <http://file.info>("~/.Rcache/e6ddd8a99035bdcfd337437a930ba19b.Rcache"))

reports.  Let us know the output and we take it from there.

/Henrik

