Hi Jen.

I have used aroma.affymetrix on HT_HG-U133_Plus_PM arrays previously
without issues.  I'll take a quick stab and if that doesn't work,
we'll have to investigate further.

Usually when the numbers in the ChipEffectSet are all zero, it means
that the files were created, but the fits weren't actually run or at
least didn't get output.  Did the running get interrupted maybe?

Anyways, to run it again and make sure it re-fits, run:

fit(plmTr, force=TRUE, verbose=verbose)

... then try and retrieve your ChipEffectSet and call
extractDataFrame().

Cheers,
Mark

