Ok, the line:

  "Installing/updating: CRAN:aroma.core (>= 1.1.0)"

was the clue.  That package is supposed to be installed from braju.com <http://braju.com>
(and not CRAN), because it is still not available for OSX on CRAN.  It
turns out that I've fixed this a while ago but uploaded the hbLite.R
script to the wrong place.

It should all work now as expected.

/Henrik

